WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.731
This is the Section 504 Court Filing Dispatch.

00:00:03.681 --> 00:00:09.909
From this page, private prosecution informations are filed to every superior court registry across Canada.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.875
Seventeen courts.

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:13.840
Federal and provincial.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.704
Section 504 of the Criminal Code.

00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:25.874
Any person who, on reasonable grounds, believes that a person has committed an indictable offence... may lay an information in writing and under oath before a justice.

00:00:25.874 --> 00:00:28.136
That is not a legal theory.

00:00:28.136 --> 00:00:29.840
That is the law.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.431
Two hundred and seventy-one officials identified from public government records.

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:38.579
Three hundred and fourteen potential Criminal Code charges documented.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:40.386
Breach of trust.

00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:42.522
Obstruction of justice.

00:00:42.522 --> 00:00:44.840
Fraud over five thousand.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.545
Intimidation.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:47.897
Treason.

00:00:47.897 --> 00:00:49.477
Sabotage.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:51.647
Three named respondents.

00:00:51.647 --> 00:00:54.886
Captain Rebecca Covey of CFNIS.

00:00:54.886 --> 00:00:57.693
Crown Prosecutor Vicky Jahye Bae.

00:00:57.693 --> 00:01:01.284
General Jennie Carignan, then Chief of Defence Staff.

00:01:01.284 --> 00:01:10.511
Each charge sourced from Hansard, Auditor General reports, Elections Canada filings, Commissioner of Lobbying records, MPCC reports, and court documents.

00:01:10.511 --> 00:01:18.624
The filing system generates cover letters, tracks delivery status, and provides sworn information templates for every court jurisdiction in Canada.

00:01:18.624 --> 00:01:20.613
This is the mechanism.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.988
Use it.
